# TagExplorer Daily Log

## Tag Tree Development — Day 3

### Tasks / Topics Covered

- Simplified overall tag hierarchy  
  - Removed 4th-level nodes (`SubStep`) to make navigation cleaner and reduce visual complexity  
  - Insight: Three levels (Module → Process → Step) are sufficient for clarity and maintainability  

- Implemented tag reordering with persistent storage  
  - Added logic to save new order directly into `view.ini` after drag-and-drop or arrow button reordering  
  - Insight: Keeping ordering logic in configuration maintains flexibility and avoids frequent code changes  

- Introduced optional `Group` property in `view.ini`  
  - Purpose: Allow logical grouping of related processes or steps without nesting folders too deeply  
  - Insight: This approach improves organization while keeping folder structure shallow and easier to manage  

### Insights & Reflections

- Simplifying structure improves usability and reduces maintenance burden  
- Logical grouping in `view.ini` is more scalable than physical subfolders  
- Reordering persisted through configuration opens path for versioned views or per-user preferences  

### Next Steps

- Display group headers in the tag tree view  
- Allow collapsing/expanding of groups dynamically  
- Explore serialization of visual state (expanded nodes, selection) to user preferences file 